{
  "name" : "Ferreira2003_CML_generation2",
  "description" : "<notes xmlns=\"http://www.sbml.org/sbml/level2/version3\">      <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">        <p>The model should reproduce the figure 2F of the article.</p>        <p>The equation 7 has been split into equations 7a-7c, in order to take into account the different flux rates of Lysine and CML formation from Schiff.</p>        <p>The model was tested in Jarnac (SBML L2 V1) and Copasi (SBML L2 V3).</p>        <br />        <p>To the extent possible under law, all copyright and related or neighbouring rights to this encoded model have been dedicated to the public domain worldwide. Please refer to      <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" title=\"Creative Commons CC0\">CC0 Public Domain Dedication</a>          for more information.      </p>      <p>In summary, you are entitled to use this encoded model in absolutely any manner you deem suitable, verbatim, or with modification, alone or embedded it in a larger context, redistribute it, commercially or not, in a restricted way or not.</p>      <br />      <p>To cite BioModels Database, please use:      <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20587024\" target=\"_blank\">Li C, Donizelli M, Rodriguez N, Dharuri H, Endler L, Chelliah V, Li L, He E, Henry A, Stefan MI, Snoep JL, Hucka M, Le Novère N, Laibe C (2010) BioModels Database: An enhanced, curated and annotated resource for published quantitative kinetic models. BMC Syst Biol., 4:92.</a>  </p></body></notes>",
  "format" : {
